  "primary_sources": {
    "status": "verified primary facts used by the initial profiles; no full manual redistribution",
    "date": "2026-10-19",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Intel SDM093 Volume4, section2.13 and inherited model tables",
        "url": "https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/intel-sdm.html",
        "manual_sha256": "79f54b67b9bb3836856f04e0c45f50406c4d4b932c64800eb788b6b705a83dbd",
        "facts": [
          "Haswell family6 models3C/45/46 use platform ratio15:8 at100MHz as reference, separately from active C0 frequency.",
          "Model RAPL energy uses606 unit exponent12:8,611 package and639 PP0 finite32bit counters. PP0 covers package cores.",
          "DTS19C valid31 and distance22:16 combine with target1A2[23:16]; current status differs from sticky history.",
          "BIOS_SIGN_ID8B revision is high32 and its documented read/latch uses zero preload plusCPUID1. This is not an update operation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "AMD PPR55898 revision0.50, Family19h Model01h B1, Volume1",
        "url": "https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/55898_B1_pub_0_50",
        "download": "https://docs.amd.com/api/khub/documents/jLTHnOp79OI4cgrwEeNL9w/content",
        "archive_sha256": "fe0f39afbf19d1a128d51605f9b958a861608daf7f04a1c1b8ca5a36cb73f534",
        "volume1_sha256": "342a3a9437fbcb4ebe1d3542f673cd69c573feee2d7850e550b75f65f60a744d",
        "facts": [
          "CPUID revision B1 is stepping1 for this exact family/model. PATCH_LEVEL8B is read only and low32.",
          "APERF/MPERF count actual/P0 C0 clocks. Interrupts must be excluded across the read pair; overflow invalidates frequency. The documented50MHz accuracy also has an instruction-spacing condition, which this implementation does not claim.",
          "Pstate0 bit63 enables its reference; CoreCOF is FID[7:0]/DFSID[13:8] times200MHz.",
          "Energy unitC0010299 exponent12:8 and coreC001029A/packageC001029B use low32 on this exact profile.",
          "This MSR profile supplies no measured AMD temperature. No Tctl/Tdie offset is guessed.",
          "PStateDef valid-value table admits FID10h..FFh, DFSID08h..1Ah then even1Ch..2Ch. Apply its conservative bound despite surrounding prose mentioning higher core dividers; below400MHz is unsupported."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "AMD energy driver scope notes",
        "url": "https://github.com/amd/amd_energy/blob/master/README.md",
        "facts": [
          "Core energy can be shared by SMT siblings. Use known domain leaders to avoid duplicate sums.",
          "Newer AMD families may have64bit counters; the initial32bit profile is not generalized."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "implementation_limits": [
      "Model predicates and unit/cache arithmetic are host-fixture qualified; only virtual-unavailable behavior is qualified on the local KVM guest.",
      "Finite energy counters are not accumulated totals or watts. A descending counter remains wrap-or-reset ambiguous.",
      "Actual read-pair values/stamps are retained; only compatible nonoverflowing1ms..10s intervals and a known equal reference admit active Hz."
    ]
  },
